## 🟦 7. Smart Contract & Security

The ShibaWave smart contract is designed with transparency, security, and community trust as top priorities.

🟦 Deployment & Verification

Deployed via Pump.fun: The ShibaWave contract is launched on the Solana blockchain using Pump.fun, ensuring a fair and open launch accessible to all participants.

Immutable / Renounced Ownership: Once deployed, the contract ownership is either renounced or strictly limited, preventing unauthorized changes and ensuring no future tampering.

Open Verification on Solscan: All transactions, token balances, and contract code can be publicly verified on Solscan. This allows anyone to inspect the contract and confirm total supply, transfers, and liquidity status.

🟦 Security Principles

Contract Transparency:
All aspects of the ShibaWave contract are visible on-chain, including token distribution, liquidity locks, and supply mechanisms. This ensures that every transaction is fully auditable.

Holder Visibility:
The community can track holders, token movements, and staking participation in real-time. This visibility builds trust and ensures fair participation.

Anti-Rug Measures:
Liquidity is locked, and no hidden minting or private allocation exists. These measures protect holders from potential rug pulls or unfair manipulation of the token supply.

🟦 Conclusion

ShibaWave’s smart contract architecture prioritizes safety, transparency, and decentralization, ensuring that the project operates fairly and securely while fostering a trusted community-driven ecosystem.
